# viem.swift

An easy to use web3 library to interact with EVM compatible chains. This project tries to resemble the API structure of the (viem)[https:viem.sh] project but in Swift.

```swift
import Viem

let client = createPublicClient(chain: .sepolia)

let address: WalletAddress = "0xA765C6AE85586572D67F1d6D2b8C30032040365E"
let balance: BigUInt = try await client.getBalance(address)

print("Mom, I'm rich: \(balance)!")
```

The best documentation can be found using intellisense. I try to expand on this in the future, but if you hit a roadblock, try reading up on the official viem docs.

## WalletAddress

This is just a `typealias` for a string, to prevent casting hell.
It supports a few additional methods:

* `"0x...".isValidWalletAddress() -> Bool`
* `"0x...".toChecksumAddress() -> WalletAddress`

## BigUInt

This is also just a `typealias` for a string, to make printing easier. I've decided to roll my own BigInt implementation to avoid dependencies and only implement what is really needed.
New features will be added when needed (or you can just extend the `BigUInt` struct to your liking.

## Clients

You set up new clients similarly to the original viem.

* `createPublicClient(chain: Chains) -> PublicClient`
* `createWalletClient(chain: Chains, account: WalletAccount) -> WalletClient`
* `privateKeyToAccount("SECRET KEY") -> WalletAccount`

When you would like to know the difference between the clients, read up on the official viem website.
Currently, the only supported way to interact with an account on chain is by supplying a private key, sorry.
																										
Note: This project is created and developed independently of the viem project.
